WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.248 --> 00:00:02.324
(gentle music)

00:00:02.324 --> 00:00:05.829
- [Narrator] This is the Guthega Skink.

00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:07.190
Small in size,

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:10.372
the Guthega Skink is
covered in camouflage skin

00:00:10.372 --> 00:00:12.198
to blend in with the alpine rocks

00:00:12.198 --> 00:00:13.448
they call home.

00:00:14.293 --> 00:00:17.739
The Guthega Skink is native
to Victoria, Australia,

00:00:17.739 --> 00:00:20.155
and can only be found in one area

00:00:20.155 --> 00:00:23.231
known as the Bogong High Plains.

00:00:23.231 --> 00:00:26.017
Because they are only
found in such a small area,

00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:28.205
they are vulnerable to natural disasters,

00:00:28.205 --> 00:00:29.788
such as bush fires,

00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:32.431
but this isn't the only threat

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:34.568
facing the skinks.

00:00:34.568 --> 00:00:36.450
Their habitat has also been affected

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.788
by the construction of ski resorts

00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:41.997
and the grazing and
trampling from farm animals,

00:00:41.997 --> 00:00:44.735
but their biggest threat
is climate change.

00:00:44.735 --> 00:00:47.534
Warmer temperatures have
allowed new predators,

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:49.636
once kept at bay by the cold,

00:00:49.636 --> 00:00:52.852
into their previously isolated habitat.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.419
Zoos Victoria have been working

00:00:54.419 --> 00:00:55.769
on a breeding program

00:00:55.769 --> 00:00:58.634
to ensure the preservation of this species

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.780
and a rescue and recovery program

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.300
if there is an immediate threat

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.217
to the wild population.

00:01:05.094 --> 00:01:07.198
This is the Guthega Skink.

00:01:07.198 --> 00:01:09.781
(gentle music)

00:01:10.994 --> 00:01:14.494
(gentle electronic music)

